<p>The company has realigned its financial segments reporting to provide stockholders with what it terms as more useful information. The segments are hospitality and attractions, broadcasting and music and cable networks. In addition, the financial statements now reflect the company's unallocated corporate expenses, all of which were previously allocated to the company's financial reporting segments. The first quarter of 1996 results have been restated to reflect the  new classification.</p>
